            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0735" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the High Commissioner
                        at Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-04T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>104. Your 587, undated.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d739-f1"/> Department informed Red
                    Cross has now made available for relief of Russian refugees in Constantinople
                    district, approximately $800,000.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
